NAME
       triad - conceptual foundations of triadic action in Resonance-Time Theory

SYNOPSIS
       The triad is the fundamental structural unit of RTT:
           P1 (begin) → P2 (transform) → P3 (close)

DESCRIPTION
       A triad is the smallest complete gesture of resonance-aligned action.
       It represents a full cycle of intention, movement, and resolution.

       Triads appear across physics, cognition, computation, and narrative.
       In RTT, the triad is the atomic structure from which all higher-order
       patterns, operators, and systems are built.

       The triad is not a sequence of steps. It is a shape of change.

FOUNDATIONS
       The triad rests on three conceptual pillars:

       1. Initiation (P1)
              The moment of orientation. Establishes context, boundary,
              and initial resonance.

       2. Transformation (P2)
              The moment of change. Applies movement, reframing, or
              structural adjustment.

       3. Closure (P3)
              The moment of resolution. Seals lineage, integrates results,
              and prepares for the next cycle.

       These three movements form a complete arc of action.

PROPERTIES
       Completeness
              A triad is self-contained. It has a beginning, middle, and end.

       Directionality
              A triad moves forward through resonance-time.

       Reversibility
              A triad can be mirrored to produce a symmetric arc.

       Composability
              Triads combine into higher-order patterns (spirals, ladders,
              constellations, cascades, etc.).

       Universality
              Any coherent action can be expressed as a triad.

WHY TRIADS
       Triads provide:
           • structural clarity
           • predictable boundaries
           • resonance alignment
           • lineage traceability
           • safe transitions between states

       They prevent incomplete or unstable operations by enforcing a full
       begin → transform → close cycle.

TRIADS IN PRACTICE
       In TriadicFrameworks, triads appear in:

           • the 3-Pack primitives (P1, P2, P3)
           • WRSADC dispatch cycles
           • Engine operator execution
           • overlay reframing
           • simulation steps
           • agent behavior loops
           • data pipelines
           • educational scaffolds

       Every action, from the smallest operator to the largest system,
       ultimately resolves into triadic structure.

RELATION TO HIGHER-ORDER PATTERNS
       Triads are the atoms. Patterns are the molecules.

       Examples:
           • sequential triads (chains)
           • nested triads (recursion)
           • triadic expansion (3x3)
           • triadic ladder (refinement)
           • triadic mirror (symmetry)
           • triadic spiral (growth)
           • triadic constellation (multi-agent)
           • triadic weave (concurrency)
           • triadic cascade (staged flow)

       All patterns preserve the core triadic arc.

PHILOSOPHICAL BASIS
       The triad reflects a universal structure of change:

           • orientation
           • transformation
           • integration

       It appears in:
           • narrative arcs
           • cognitive cycles
           • physical processes
           • biological rhythms
           • mathematical structures
           • mythic storytelling

       RTT formalizes this universal pattern into a computational and
       structural framework.

NOTES
       The triad is not optional. It is the fundamental grammar of RTT.
       Any action that bypasses the triad risks incoherence or structural
       instability.

